#
# Clean conformance fixture for math:ProbabilityValueRangeShape (Rule P1): a framed exact
# math:ProbabilityValue in the closed unit interval [0, 1]. Following the exact-rational
# discipline (AC#6), the exact magnitude 0.72 is carried as a math:RationalValue 18/25
# (math:numerator/math:denominator) rather than a decimal, so it also satisfies
# math:RationalValueShape (integer numerator, non-zero integer denominator). It names its
# gmeow:hasReferenceFrame (P3), is not typed math:OddsValue / math:LogOddsValue (P2), and
# carries no logic:confidence (P10). It MUST raise NO probability failure class.
# Positive counterpart of counter-examples/probability-value-above-unit.ttl.
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecProbabilityValueInUnit).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:inUnitProbability a math:ProbabilityValue , math:RationalValue ;
    math:numerator 18 ;        # 18/25 = 0.72, within the closed unit interval [0, 1]
    math:denominator 25 ;
    gmeow:hasReferenceFrame ex:forecastFrame .

ex:forecastFrame a gmeow:ReferenceFrame .
<http://example.org/math/inUnitProbability> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasDimension> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dimensionless> .
